<h2 id="ha-ctrl-015-acceptance">Acceptance and evidence</h2>

1. Test a timestamped snapshot, an unknown capture time, a loading stream, a playable stream, a stalled stream and denied access. No stale image may keep a Live label.
2. Compare the entity’s Idle, Streaming or Recording state, where reported, with the viewer. Do not infer recording from a feed, or from the state not being Idle.
3. Test keyboard playback, fullscreen and exit, focus return, control contrast on varied frames, and any motion or audio controls.
4. Check shared-display content and public evidence for real faces, addresses, tokens and private URLs. Check that retrying or closing the viewer does not change privacy or recording.

Record what was tested using [Native task accessibility and evidence](native-task-accessibility.html). A source review or a local example is not a live-device check.

